<div class="md-shell md-shell--org">
  {{!-- BASIC VIEW'S ORG NAV (2026-09-25, requested). Selecting an organisation used to REPLACE
       the rail with the two-item `ch-tabs` strip below, so the section you had just entered was
       the one place in Basic with no sidebar. The rail renders here too now, in org mode: see
       `orgSection` in components/dashboard/classic-rail.js for what changes and why.
       `@org={{this.model}}` is what puts it in that mode -- the directory page mounts the same
       component with no argument and is unchanged.
       A DIRECT CHILD OF `.md-shell`, for the two reasons templates/organizations.hbs records at
       its own mount: `.md-shell` carries the page's gradient, so a rail outside it would sit on
       bare page; and `.md-shell > .md-workspace` is a DIRECT-CHILD selector that a flex wrapper
       between the two would silently break. --}}
  {{#if this.isClassic}}
    <Dashboard::ClassicRail @org={{this.model}} />
  {{/if}}
  <div class="md-workspace">
    {{!-- BASIC VIEW REPLACES THE PILL NAV WITH THE `ch-` TAB STRIP (requested 2026-09-23), in
         this exact slot -- the strip used to render further down, inside the page card, which is
         why hiding the pills alone left a gap and the strip in the wrong place.
         It wears `ch-tabs` / `ch-tab`, the Basic home page's own classes, so it takes the gentle
         and focused schemes from there rather than restating either.

         THE TWO STRIPS NO LONGER MIRROR EACH OTHER (2026-09-25). They were the same two items in
         two sets of class names -- a way back, and the section you are on. Basic's has since
         become the ADMIN AREA'S OWN TABS (Admin plus the five people sections; see the note on
         that branch), because Basic also gained the rail beside it, which took over both of the
         jobs that pair was doing. Modern has no such rail, so its strip is unchanged and still
         reads "< Home | <section>".
         THAT IS WHY `currentSectionLabel`, `backRoute`, `backModels` and `backLabel`
         (controllers/organization.js) are now read by the MODERN branch alone. They are still
         correct and still used; they simply have one consumer instead of two. The rule they
         carry is worth keeping in mind if Basic's strip ever needs a way back again: on the room
         DETAIL page the label reads "Back" and returns to the rooms LIST, because that is the
         page above it, and everywhere else it reads "Home" and leaves the org section. --}}
    {{#if this.isClassic}}
      {{!-- THE ADMIN AREA'S OWN TABS (2026-09-25, requested: "the ch-tabs need to be: Admin,
           Managers, Supervisors, Communicators, Evals, Symbols (instead of Home and
           Organizations)").

           IT REPLACED A "< Home | <section>" PAIR. That pair was a way back plus a label; both
           jobs now belong to the rail beside it, which carries Home Page, Organizations and the
           org's five sections and marks the page you are on. Two navs saying "where you are"
           was the redundancy this removes.

           THE FIVE PEOPLE TABS ARE ONE ROUTE WITH A PARAM, not five routes. Managers,
           Supervisors, Communicators, Evals and Symbols are sections of `organization.people`
           (templates/organization/people.hbs), selected until now by a click-only property that
           a parent template had no way to set -- see the note on `section` in
           controllers/organization/people.js for why it moved into the URL. SYMBOLS IS
           `extras`: that is the value its own tab has always used and the name of the API it
           loads (`/organizations/:id/extras`), so the label and the param differ on purpose.

           ADMIN IS `organization.index`, and it is the tab this strip lights on that page.
           The five take their highlight from `activePeopleSection`, which asks the people
           controller what it is showing rather than re-reading the URL, so the strip cannot
           disagree with the page under it -- including with no param at all, where the page
           defaults to Managers and so does this.

           NO COUNTS (requested 2026-09-25: "Remove the count from the nav menu"). They were
           carried up here from the people page's own Basic strip when this replaced it -- the
           manager/supervisor/user totals and the two used-of-allotted ratios. Each figure is
           still shown by the section it belongs to, in its own heading ("2 managers",
           "1 / 10 eval accounts used"), so nothing is lost by taking them out of the nav.
           `ch-organizations-tabs` GOES WITH THEM: that class exists only to stack a label over
           a count (`.ch-tab` becomes a flex COLUMN, _classic-home.scss:1366), which a
           single-line tab does not want. The base `.ch-tab` is the right treatment now.
           Its rules are left in place, unused -- dead CSS is its own cleanup. --}}
      <nav class="ch-tabs ch-tabs--primary" aria-label={{t "Organization Navigation" key="org_navigation"}}>
        <LinkTo @route="organization.index" @model={{this.model.id}} class="ch-tab {{if this.adminTabActive "is-active"}}" aria-current={{if this.adminTabActive "page"}}>
          <span class="ch-tab__label">{{t "Admin" key="admin"}}</span>
        </LinkTo>
        <LinkTo @route="organization.people" @model={{this.model.id}} @query={{hash section="managers"}} class="ch-tab {{if (is_equal this.activePeopleSection "managers") "is-active"}}" aria-current={{if (is_equal this.activePeopleSection "managers") "page"}}>
          <span class="ch-tab__label">{{t "Managers" key="managers"}}</span>
        </LinkTo>
        <LinkTo @route="organization.people" @model={{this.model.id}} @query={{hash section="supervisors"}} class="ch-tab {{if (is_equal this.activePeopleSection "supervisors") "is-active"}}" aria-current={{if (is_equal this.activePeopleSection "supervisors") "page"}}>
          <span class="ch-tab__label">{{t "Supervisors" key="supervisors"}}</span>
        </LinkTo>
        <LinkTo @route="organization.people" @model={{this.model.id}} @query={{hash section="communicators"}} class="ch-tab {{if (is_equal this.activePeopleSection "communicators") "is-active"}}" aria-current={{if (is_equal this.activePeopleSection "communicators") "page"}}>
          <span class="ch-tab__label">{{t "Communicators" key="communicators"}}</span>
        </LinkTo>
        <LinkTo @route="organization.people" @model={{this.model.id}} @query={{hash section="evals"}} class="ch-tab {{if (is_equal this.activePeopleSection "evals") "is-active"}}" aria-current={{if (is_equal this.activePeopleSection "evals") "page"}}>
          <span class="ch-tab__label">{{t "Evals" key="evals"}}</span>
        </LinkTo>
        <LinkTo @route="organization.people" @model={{this.model.id}} @query={{hash section="extras"}} class="ch-tab {{if (is_equal this.activePeopleSection "extras") "is-active"}}" aria-current={{if (is_equal this.activePeopleSection "extras") "page"}}>
          <span class="ch-tab__label">{{t "Symbols" key="symbols"}}</span>
        </LinkTo>
      </nav>
    {{else if this.showSectionPillNav}}
      {{!-- ...AND NOT AT ALL WHERE THE APP SHELL ALREADY DREW ONE (2026-09-23). On the rooms
           page a rooms-only supervisor gets the FULL primary nav from the app shell, with
           Rooms active, so this two-item strip would stack a second nav under the first.
           `showSectionPillNav` asks utils/primary_nav the same question the app shell asks
           before mounting its nav, so exactly one of the two renders -- see the note on that
           computed in controllers/organization.js.
           MODERN NOW MATCHES BASIC (requested 2026-09-23): a way back, and the section you are
           on, with that section marked active. It previously listed every org destination --
           Dashboard, User, Reports, Rooms, Settings and the rest -- and those are no longer
           reachable from this nav in either view.
           `is-active` plus `aria-current="page"` on a <span> rather than a link: there is
           nowhere to go, and that pairing is what tells assistive tech you are already here.
           The label comes from the router via `currentSectionLabel`, so each org sub-page names
           itself without this template knowing which child is rendering. --}}
      <nav class="md-pillnav md-pillnav--dashboard" aria-label={{t "Organization Navigation" key="org_navigation"}}>
        <LinkTo @route={{this.backRoute}} @models={{this.backModels}} class="md-pillnav__pill">
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" style="margin-right: 4px;"><polyline points="15 18 9 12 15 6"/></svg>
          {{this.backLabel}}
        </LinkTo>
        <span class="md-pillnav__pill is-active" aria-current="page">{{this.currentSectionLabel}}</span>
      </nav>
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- ORGANISATION SWITCHER, ABOVE THE HEADER (requested 2026-09-23). It sits here rather
         than inside the page card because it changes WHICH organisation the header names, so it
         has to read as being upstream of it.
         Shown only when there is more than one to choose between -- see `showOrgSwitcher`; with
         a single org it would be a dropdown whose only option is the page you are on.
         A <details>/<summary> DROPDOWN, not a native <select> (requested: the open list had to
         be on-brand, and a native select's popup is drawn by the operating system and cannot be
         themed). `<details>` keeps the toggle keyboard-operable and exposes expanded state to
         assistive tech without a custom widget's worth of ARIA and key handling -- the same
         trade `components/user-pill-nav.hbs` makes for its own collapsed menu.
         It reuses NEITHER `.ch-tabselect` NOR `.md-pillnav-dropdown`: both are `display: none`
         until 550px, where they stand in for a tab strip, so wearing either would have hidden
         this control at every normal width.
         Each option is a LinkTo, so choosing one is an ordinary navigation -- no change
         handler, and middle-click and open-in-new-tab work as they should. The trigger shows
         `model.name`, so after the transition it already reads as the newly selected org.
         `{{details-autoclose}}` closes the menu on a choice, on an outside click and on Escape:
         `<details>` keeps `open` as DOM state and this element SURVIVES the transition (only
         the parent route's model changes), so without it the menu stayed open over the page it
         had just navigated to. --}}
    {{#if this.showOrgSwitcher}}
      <div class="ch-org-switcher">
        <span class="ch-org-switcher__label" id="org-switcher-label">{{t "Available Organizations" key="accessible_orgs"}}</span>
        <details class="ch-org-dropdown" {{details-autoclose}}>
          <summary class="ch-org-dropdown__trigger" aria-label={{t "Choose an organization" key="choose_organization"}}>
            <span class="ch-org-dropdown__current">{{this.model.name}}</span>
            <svg class="ch-org-dropdown__chevron" width="12" height="8" viewBox="0 0 12 8" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M1 1.5L6 6.5L11 1.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <ul class="ch-org-dropdown__list" role="list">
            {{#each this.switchableOrgs as |org|}}
              <li>
                {{#if org.is_current}}
                  <span class="ch-org-dropdown__option is-current" aria-current="true">{{org.name}}</span>
                {{else}}
                  <LinkTo @route="organization.rooms" @model={{org.id}} class="ch-org-dropdown__option">{{org.name}}</LinkTo>
                {{/if}}
              </li>
            {{/each}}
          </ul>
        </details>
      </div>
    {{/if}}
    <header class="md-hero md-hero--dashboard md-hero--org">
      <h1 class="md-hero__title"><span class="md-hero__title--from-left">
        {{#if this.model.permissions.view}}
          {{this.model.name}}
        {{else}}
          {{t "Organization" key="organization"}}
        {{/if}}
      </span></h1>
      <span class="md-hero__divider" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <p class="md-hero__sub md-hero__sub--meta"><span class="md-hero__sub--from-right">
        <span class="md-hero-meta__item">
          <svg class="md-hero-meta__icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H8a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="12" cy="7" r="4"/></svg>
          {{t "user" key="user_count" count=this.model.total_users}}
        </span>
        {{#if this.model.total_supervisors}}
          <span class="md-hero-meta__item">
            <svg class="md-hero-meta__icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg>
            {{t "supervisor" key="supervisor_count" count=this.model.total_supervisors}}
          </span>
        {{/if}}
        <span class="md-hero-meta__item">
          <svg class="md-hero-meta__icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 20h9"/><path d="M16.5 3.5a2.121 2.121 0 0 1 3 3L7 19l-4 1 1-4L16.5 3.5z"/></svg>
          {{t "manager" key="manager_count" count=this.model.total_managers}}
        </span>
        {{#if this.model.created}}
          <span class="md-hero-meta__item" title={{date this.model.created}}>
            {{t "created" key="created_lower"}} <span class="md-hero-meta__nocap">{{date_ago this.model.created}}</span>
          </span>
        {{/if}}
      </span></p>
    </header>

    <main class="md-main md-main--org">
      {{outlet}}
    </main>
  </div>
</div>
